FEATURE: example-design-standard
DATE: 2026-08-26
SCOPE: require module example pages to be properly designed, not bare demos
FOLLOWS: changelog/auto-writer-docs

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vUX library (this repository) — conventions only.

  - CLAUDE.md   new section "Example pages (required for every module)"

No source, documentation or example file changed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT CHANGED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CLAUDE.md now requires every module's example page to be designed work rather than a
test harness with buttons: a committed visual treatment, the component leading the page
at a size that cannot be missed, live controls for every config property, a section that
demonstrates the validation errors, offline self-containment, responsiveness, and JS
commented for a reader rather than for a maintainer.

It names examples/autowriter/ as the reference implementation, and records that
examples/modal/, examples/form/ and examples/spa/ predate the standard so they are not
copied as the house pattern — with the reason they are plainer (structural behaviour
rather than a visual effect) kept alongside, so the note is not read as a verdict on them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONSEQUENCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The three older example pages are now out of step with the stated standard. They are
left as they are rather than rewritten here, since that is a substantial piece of design
work per page and belongs to its own feature entry; CLAUDE.md says to bring each up to
standard when it is next touched.
